From 4a1ff8f7a7ef39d2c7c21bcfac12a7596a0f9d52 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 02:40:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] FixedPoint solver: line search of the NewtonK0 method

Option LineSearch of the NewtonK0 method of the FixedPoint solver, the
line search by backtracking on the norm of the residual of the Newton
solver (LineSearch structure). An estimate at which the integration of the
behaviours fails is a refused trial, and the resolution fails if no step
is acceptable. With the first choice of Eisenstat and Walker, the
tolerance which follows a reduced step uses the norm of the linear model
at this step. The option is refused by the ElasticOperator and
ModifiedNewton methods, whose corrections are not the ones of an inexact
Newton method.

Without the option, the iterations are unchanged, including the estimate
moved towards the previous one when the integration fails.

FixedPointSolverTest: on the cube whose stress saturates
(NewtonLineSearchTest), NewtonK0 does not converge without line search,
and makes the reduced steps and gives the solution of the Newton solver
with it, with an assembled tangent operator or without assembly; the
tolerances of Eisenstat and Walker are computed again from the norms of
the linear model given with the information on the iterations; the option
may be enabled between two time steps.
